pected ratio is 7.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.5 to 12.8. December accounts for 8% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,988.64 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be lower than expected, or budgets might be fixed. There could be other reasons for the amounts being just under the legal threshold.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of the contracts to see if they align with the body's needs. Look at awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same type of service. Review the specific services described in contract [1] to ensure they match the stated purpose.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["PhCGmlDtkBOcTfjQf3USOg%3D%3D","zvt%2FH%2F%2BIFjzpxJFXpLZ%2B2A%3D%3D","UaZFHE78UZnN3k3tjedSGw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}